 "status": "APPROVED by Karim 2026-09-25 (07 Decision 28), with the readiness-check fixes. Self-review only (07 D17). Updated 2026-09-25 by delegation (07 Decisions 33–34): training messages tm.notAccepted and tm.notForTask added; feedback[].terminalLine added. 2026-09-25: ui.assessment.carryover reworded count-neutral (07 D39). 2026-09-26 (Phase 4 gate, 07 D42–D44): interface words added as ui.* keys and listed in 'ui' (D43); ui.what.* listed (they were in the string files but missing here); displays.AN.headerNumber added (D44).",
 "rules": [
  "Every Amadeus statement in the text files traces to a VERIFIED entry of DEIXEN_Amadeus_Verified_Reference.md (listed per lesson in 'verifiedBasis').",
  "All flights, fares, taxes, phone numbers, names, office IDs and record locators are fictional practice data. Airline code 6X is used only as a practice code; no real schedule or fare is implied.",
  "Tokens in braces are filled at runtime: {TASK_DATE}/{SCN_DATE}/{DEMO_DATE} = today + dateOffsetDays as DDMMM (English month, uppercase); {EXPECTED_ENTRY} = the task's expected entry for that step; {N} = a count.",
  "Terminal placement (07 Decisions 30, 33, 34): feedback, hints and Coach texts appear in the DEIXEN panel, never in the Terminal. feedback[].terminalLine names the training line the Terminal shows when that feedback is triggered by an entry; null = the Terminal shows a verified Amadeus message or the real result instead (ER cases per Build Spec §6 row 8), or the item is a requested hint. A more specific training message takes precedence where its condition holds: tm.noPracticeData (route without practice data), tm.classNotOffered (class shown as 0), tm.secondName (a second passenger). An entry that fails its checklist leaves the practice PNR unchanged. A training message with more than one sentence shows its first sentence in the Terminal and the rest in the panel.",
  "Tokens in interface words (07 D43): {N} = a number (lesson number, element number, entry number); {T} = total entries of a Ghost Mode script; {CMD} = one command, Latin, left-to-right; {COMMANDS} = the commands of a Ghost Mode script, joined with the interface language's list format (EN 'AN, SS and NM'; AR 'AN وSS وNM'); {K} = one key-row character (/ or -). ui.lang.en and ui.lang.ar are the same in both files: each language's name is always written in that language."
 ],
